### File Handling & Input output managment

## File handling:- 

-File handling is the way a program interacts with files on your computer. It involves creating, reading, writing, updating, and deleting files.
Key Points to Remember

. File Handling allows a program to store, read, write, and update data permanently.
. Data stored in variables is lost when the program ends; files keep it safe.
. There are two main types of file handling in Java:
. Byte-Based Streams - for binary data (images, PDFs, audio)
. Character-Based Streams - for text data (logs, notes, CSV)
· Use classes like:
. FilelnputStream, FileOutputStream (for byte-based)
. FileReader, FileWriter (for character-based)
. Always use loops to read/write and close the file when done.
. Use try-catch blocks to handle errors.
. Prefer try-with-resources to automatically close files.

